--
libstdc++ 13 <format>: std::format("{}", 42) is converted without dropping a
system-header body.  The verification (test_format.desc) is THOROUGH.
broken-libstdcxx16: with libstdc++ 16 (16-20260315), _M_reserve and _M_span
of _Seq_sink lose their bodies: std::string::iterator is not
random_access_iterator, so span<char> cannot be made from the string
(KNOWNBUG cpp20_hidden_friend_spaceship_template_alias_return_type).
The drops of __should_escape_ascii and __write_escaped_char are fixed
(cpp20_is_constant_evaluated_forwarded_through_constexpr_function).
